@startuml 18-gate-and-queue
!include style.iuml
title The Gate and the Retrieval queue
start
:Gate frees\n(a section ended, pause taken);
:Pick the best tier waiting\nfirst come, first served inside a tier;
note right
  1 new_day   Discovery: days since last Run
  2 detail    Discovery: a new project's detail
  3 fresh     Retrieval: never-read project
  4 refresh   Retrieval: timeline re-read
  5 history   Discovery: past-year backfill
end note
:Section runs - ONE request in flight;
if (429 or 403?) then (yes)
  :Gate LATCHED\nevery caller is refused without touching e-GP;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:Pause 4 to 6 s\n(skipped if nothing else can ask e-GP);
:Retrieval worker calls queue.pick();
if (Never-read project waiting?) then (yes)
  if (Waiting-room place free?) then (yes)
    :Take newest-announcement fresh project\nholding a place;
  else (no)
    :Serve a refresh that needs no place\n(oldest check first);
  endif
else (no)
  :Serve a refresh (oldest check first);
endif
if (Anything takeable?) then (no)
  :waitForWork()\nwakes on: new work, Discovery ended,\na place freed, or a stop;
else (yes)
endif
stop
@enduml
